<Base title="Courses" description="Free, openly shared ecology courses by Aiyu Zheng: Rediscovering Agroforestry, Plants and People, and Introduction to Ecological Thinking.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="page-title">
      <h1>Courses</h1>
      <p class="lede">Below, you’ll find a collection of ecology and related courses that I have created with the intention of providing free public access. I invite you to use or modify these courses for your own classrooms but kindly remember to give appropriate credit to me as the original creator.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="section split">
      <div>
        <h2>Rediscovering Agroforestry</h2>
        <p><strong>From ancient homegardens through colonial disruption, to the rediscovery of practices never truly lost.</strong></p>
        <p>This course is currently under development and explores the history of sustainable agroforestry before the rise of monoculture, along with the future of agroforestry and sustainable agriculture. An accompanying <strong><a href="https://aiyuz.github.io/agroforestry" target="_blank" rel="noopener">interactive teaching website</a></strong> provides readings, visualizations, and hands-on exercises for use both in the classroom and as independent assignments.</p>
      </div>
      <a href="https://aiyuz.github.io/agroforestry" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="border:0"><img class="card-img" src="/uploads/2026/06/Screenshot-2026-06-26-at-12.50.23-PM.jpg" alt="Screenshot of the Rediscovering Agroforestry teaching website" loading="lazy" /></a>
    </section>

    <section class="section split">
      <img class="card-img" src="/uploads/2023/10/IMGP4085-scaled.jpg" alt="Terraced fields in Guizhou, China" loading="lazy" />
      <div>
        <h2>Plants and People</h2>
        <p><strong>Ecological Dialogues Across Civilizations</strong></p>
        <p>In summer 2025, I taught this course in person at Veritas China Summer School. Designed as an introduction to liberal arts education through the lens of ecology, it is intended for students interested in environmental disciplines and the intersections among biology, environmental studies, anthropology, and sustainable development.</p>
        <div class="file-row">
          <a class="btn" href="/uploads/2026/06/草木生态学讲义_watermark.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Lecture notes 草木生态学讲义 (PDF)</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section split">
      <div>
        <h2>Introduction to Ecological Thinking</h2>
        <p><strong>Deciphering patterns and processes</strong></p>
        <p>An undergraduate course I designed to introduce ecological thinking with a focus on connecting ecological questions to different ecological methods with a flipped classroom format. It will be available online for public access.</p>
        <p>In summer 2024, I offered this course in Mandarin online in collaboration with <a href="https://www.veritaschina.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Veritas China</a>, a student-led organization promoting liberal arts education. You can check out the themed teaching notes for the course below.</p>
        <p><strong style="color: var(--amber)">The link to English contents and recorded lectures in this course will be available soon!</strong></p>
